99
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:20,380
And then he looked at positive words, positive research.

100
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:29,440
He looked for research on joy, and he found a staggering 415 studies.

101
00:13:29,900 --> 00:13:40,440
It does get better. He looked at research on happiness, and he found close to 2,000 articles on happiness in 33 years.

102
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:46,460
Life satisfaction came out top, over 2,500 studies.

103
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:55,920
Still, if you look at that, the negative studies versus the positive studies, the ratio that you get is 21 to 1.

104
00:13:56,720 --> 00:14:12,400
For every one article on some positive aspect, some positive element of life, well-being, satisfaction, joy, happiness, you get 21 articles on depression, anxiety, schizophrenia, neurosis, and so on.

105
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:16,160
Ratio of 21 to 1.

106
00:14:16,620 --> 00:14:19,180
Very depressing ratio, I must admit.

107
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:23,560
In fact, it makes me very angry and anxious.

108
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:36,280
studies focus on primarily on what doesn't work mostly on what doesn't work and this is not a new

109
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:43,500
phenomenon here is um something from abraham maslow whom we mentioned last time talking about

110
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:51,900
this phenomenon in 1954 the science of psychology has been far more successful on the negative than

111
00:14:51,900 --> 00:14:57,640
on the positive side it has revealed to us much more about man's shortcomings his illnesses

112
00:14:57,640 --> 00:15:07,320
his sins, but little about his potentialities, his virtues, his achievable aspirations, or his psychological height.

113
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:13,980
