a study that was more recent. This was published in 2004, Harvard Crimson. And the article

145
00:19:04,650 --> 00:19:13,950
says that in their six-month study of this, 80% of Harvard students experienced depression

146
00:19:13,950 --> 00:19:24,810
over the past year. Now, we're not talking about the regular ups and downs that most people have 10 times a day. I certainly do. We're talking about depression here for an extended

147
00:19:24,810 --> 00:19:33,830
period of time, 47% of Harvard students, according to this, and granted, this is not an academic

148
00:19:33,830 --> 00:19:39,490
study, but I will share with you an academic study in a minute, published in a top-tier

