00:19:41,770 --> 00:19:52,210
But what the Crimson has found in its survey is that 47% of Harvard students over the past year have experienced depression to the point of not functioning.

151
00:19:53,250 --> 00:19:57,870
So really so that they couldn't leave a home, they were really struggling to just basically get through the day.

152
00:19:59,330 --> 00:19:59,730
47%.

153
00:20:01,130 --> 00:20:06,570
Now when people look at this, they say, well, of course, we need to focus more on psychopathology. 21 to 1, not enough.

154
00:20:06,930 --> 00:20:09,170
30 to 1 sounds more like it.

155
00:20:13,090 --> 00:20:17,370
We see it around campuses. This is not peculiar to Harvard.

156
00:20:18,890 --> 00:20:20,730
Not at all peculiar to Harvard.

157
00:20:21,450 --> 00:20:24,390
Richard Caddison, who's the head of the mental health services here,

158
00:20:25,190 --> 00:20:35,770
in the New England Journal of Medicine, probably a V-leading journal in the field of medicine, recently published an article where he talked about a survey that was done

