00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:17,540
Shouldn't it even be increased?

176
00:22:18,620 --> 00:22:23,400
How can we even think about studying happiness and well-being and love and joy?

177
00:22:25,730 --> 00:22:34,150
Shouldn't we first deal with the real pressing problem of depression, anxiety, neurosis, and so on?

178
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:41,840
Some truth to that, but again, what I'm going to argue for in this class is that we do need to also,

179
00:22:41,980 --> 00:22:48,340
not only, not exclusively, not even necessarily primarily, we need to also focus on the positive.

180
00:22:49,060 --> 00:22:57,000
I'm going to talk about three reasons why we should do that. The first reason is that it is important to focus on what works

181
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:06,400
because what works or what we focus on, rather, creates reality. And if we focus on what is working, we'll have more working in our world,

182
00:23:06,620 --> 00:23:09,880
more working in ourselves, more working in our relationships.

183
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:22,580
The second reason why positive psychology as an independent field of study, as a course in and of itself is important, is that being happy is not just the negation of happiness.

184
00:23:22,780 --> 00:23:31,340
It doesn't mean that if I just get rid of depression or anxiety that I'm experiencing, I spontaneously become happy. That's not the case. That's not how it works.

185
00:23:32,940 --> 00:23:38,100
And finally, prevention, which is very important today,

